t block I11 to prevent O’s win next turn.  \n\nThus the only logical move now is **I11** to block O’s four to become five.  \n\nThat is a forced defensive move.  \n\nBut maybe Black can also make a threat while blocking?  \n\nCheck: If Black plays I11, O’s vertical four is blocked.  \nThen Black’s threats: Black could then threaten at C8? But not immediate win.  \n\nGiven all, best move is block I11, then next turn try to make own threat.  \n\nActually, let’s check if Black has any immediate win overlooked:  \n\nWhat about **J8**? That’s empty. Does it connect to anything?  \nFrom J8 horizontally: I8=O, J8=X, K8 empty — no.  \nDiagonally: Not making five.  \n\nNo, so no immediate win.  \n\nSo conclusion:  \nNo winning move for Black right now; must block O’s vertical four at I11.  \n\n---\n\n**Evaluation:**  \nNo immediate winning move for Black; O has a potential win next move at I11, so Black must block.  \n\n**Reason:**  \nO has four vertical stones I7–I10, open at I11. If Black doesn’t block I11, O wins next turn. No other immediate lethal threat for Black to exploit, so defensive move is forced.  \n\n**Answer:**  \n\n```json\n{"col": "I", "row": 11}\n```'}
